You mentioned that you have a dataset that contains the distance and time for each route, and you are currently using a Python script that calculates the efficiency of each route by dividing the distance by the time. However, you mentioned that this method is not very accurate, as the time data is not consistent in terms of units (some routes are measured in hours, while others are measured in minutes).

To address this issue, I recommend using a different approach that takes into account the differences in time units. One way to do this is to convert all time values to the same unit before calculating the efficiency. For example, if some routes are measured in hours and others are measured in minutes, you can convert all of them to minutes.

